WEBVTT

NOTE Episode: The Borrowed Pouch

1
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:24.319
<v Old Timber>There is room beside the flat stone today, little ones. Bongo tested it for sitting and reports that it stayed exactly where he left it.</v>

2
00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:30.069
<v Old Timber>Picture being sure you know what happened while your friend is just as sure of something different.</v>

3
00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:39.656
<v Old Timber>Anger is a real feeling. God can help us notice it without letting it choose cruel words, sharp guesses, or a story that was never proved.</v>

4
00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:47.086
<v Old Timber>One afternoon, Quilla the chinchilla asked Chitter the chipmunk to lend her his small woven pouch.</v>

5
00:00:47.436 --> 00:00:55.476
<v Old Timber>It was a little thing. But little things sometimes carry breakfast, memories, and rather more trust than their size suggests.</v>

6
00:00:56.176 --> 00:01:02.833
<v Quilla>Chitter, may I borrow your pouch until the sun reaches the tall oak? I need both paws for the burr patch.</v>

7
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:09.223
<v Chitter>The brown one? My good brown one? The one with the neat corner and the knot that only looks worried?</v>

8
00:01:09.573 --> 00:01:10.485
<v Quilla>That one.</v>

9
00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:17.828
<v Chitter>It holds seeds, string, one polished pebble, and backup string in case the first string needs backup.</v>

10
00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.394
<v Quilla>I will disturb none of their duties.</v>

11
00:01:20.744 --> 00:01:28.156
<v Chitter>All right. Yes. I trust you. Back on the forked branch beside the flat stone before the oak-shadow reaches it.</v>

12
00:01:28.506 --> 00:01:38.067
<v Quilla>Forked branch. Flat stone. Before the shadow. I will put it there myself.</v>

13
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:44.857
<v Chitter>My aunt helped me weave it. The worried knot was the first knot I tied without her holding the string.</v>

14
00:01:45.207 --> 00:01:51.798
<v Quilla>Then I am borrowing something loved, not only something useful. I will take care of both parts.</v>

15
00:01:52.148 --> 00:01:59.068
<v Old Timber>Bongo the bear cub came backward through the grass, dragging a fallen branch twice as wide as his plan.</v>

16
00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:08.401
<v Bongo>I got this! It is going to be a shade frame. At present it is mostly a branch with ambition.</v>

17
00:02:08.751 --> 00:02:13.779
<v Chitter>Not that forked branch. My return branch is the smaller one by the stone.</v>

18
00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:19.848
<v Bongo>Understood. Two branches. One ambitious. One employed in returning.</v>

19
00:02:20.198 --> 00:02:26.878
<v Old Timber>Garingo the parrot dropped from the willow wearing a round leaf on his chest like an official badge.</v>

20
00:02:27.228 --> 00:02:37.531
<v Garingo>BEHOLD! A loan. A deadline. A branch of return. This moment requires a careful witness with excellent feathers.</v>

21
00:02:37.881 --> 00:02:40.281
<v Quilla>It requires me to bring back a pouch.</v>

22
00:02:40.631 --> 00:02:43.049
<v Garingo>And someone to announce that you did.</v>

23
00:02:43.399 --> 00:02:49.679
<v Old Timber>Zippy the hummingbird arrived with three leaf cards already labelled BEFORE, DURING, and AFTER.</v>

24
00:02:50.029 --> 00:02:55.542
<v Zippy>Wait - wait. I made a timeline in case the borrowing starts needing a timeline.</v>

25
00:02:55.892 --> 00:02:59.292
<v Chitter>It is a pouch, Zippy. It will not grow chapters.</v>

26
00:02:59.642 --> 00:03:02.382
<v Zippy>That sounds like BEFORE talking.</v>

27
00:03:02.732 --> 00:03:09.732
<v Old Timber>Shelly the young tortoise reached the flat stone and looked at the six creatures preparing for one small loan.</v>

28
00:03:10.082 --> 00:03:12.824
<v Shelly>The pouch has already formed a committee.</v>

29
00:03:13.174 --> 00:03:19.501
<v Garingo>A witness is not a committee. A witness is the complete truth wearing a badge.</v>

30
00:03:19.851 --> 00:03:21.378
<v Shelly>A leaf badge.</v>

31
00:03:21.728 --> 00:03:24.561
<v Garingo>A grand badge must begin somewhere.</v>

32
00:03:24.911 --> 00:03:31.671
<v Old Timber>Quilla tucked the pouch beneath one arm and walked toward the burr patch while Chitter watched the knot disappear.</v>

33
00:03:32.021 --> 00:03:36.909
<v Chitter>Forked branch. Flat stone. Before the shadow.</v>

34
00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:38.428
<v Quilla>I heard you.</v>

35
00:03:38.778 --> 00:03:47.804
<v Old Timber>At the burr patch, Quilla worked one seed head at a time. She kept Chitter's pouch tucked high, away from every catching hook.</v>

36
00:03:48.154 --> 00:03:54.591
<v Quilla>Seeds in my basket. String in its pocket. Pebble exactly where Chitter left it.</v>

37
00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:59.191
<v Garingo>Witness note: borrower has resisted a polished pebble.</v>

38
00:03:59.541 --> 00:04:01.189
<v Quilla>It is a pebble.</v>

39
00:04:01.539 --> 00:04:05.679
<v Garingo>A polished pebble. The witness record will show restraint.</v>

40
00:04:06.392 --> 00:04:14.239
<v Old Timber>Before the oak-shadow touched the stone, Chitter returned. The flat stone was there. The forked branch was not.</v>

41
00:04:14.589 --> 00:04:22.709
<v Chitter>No branch. No pouch. No neat corner, no worried knot, no backup string for the other backup string.</v>

42
00:04:23.059 --> 00:04:29.905
<v Garingo>Remain calm. Your official witness observed the return with both eyes and most of one beak.</v>

43
00:04:30.255 --> 00:04:35.294
<v Chitter>You saw Quilla put it here? On this branch? Beside this stone?</v>

44
00:04:35.644 --> 00:04:45.524
<v Garingo>I saw pouch, branch, and Quilla. I announced, RETURN OBSERVED. The evidence received excellent projection.</v>

45
00:04:45.874 --> 00:04:46.930
<v Chitter>Then where is it?</v>

46
00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.597
<v Old Timber>Quilla came through the grass with three burrs in her fur and no pouch beneath her arm.</v>

47
00:04:52.947 --> 00:04:57.367
<v Quilla>You are early. I returned it before the shadow reached the stone.</v>

48
00:04:57.717 --> 00:04:59.178
<v Chitter>It is not here.</v>

49
00:04:59.528 --> 00:05:04.695
<v Quilla>I put it on the fork of the branch myself. Gah-Ring-Goh saw me.</v>

50
00:05:05.045 --> 00:05:11.033
<v Garingo>Confirmed. Signed by a leaf badge and a voice that carries across water.</v>

51
00:05:11.383 --> 00:05:19.423
<v Chitter>You put it somewhere, maybe. But not here, because here is empty, and I asked you three times where here was.</v>

52
00:05:19.773 --> 00:05:23.743
<v Quilla>You asked once. I repeated it once. I returned it once.</v>

53
00:05:24.093 --> 00:05:26.613
<v Chitter>Then how can your returned pouch be gone?</v>

54
00:05:26.963 --> 00:05:34.123
<v Chitter>That knot is the first one my aunt taught me to tie. If the pouch is gone, I cannot make that first knot happen again.</v>

55
00:05:34.473 --> 00:05:37.728
<v Quilla>It is your pouch. And I do not know.</v>

56
00:05:38.078 --> 00:05:42.874
<v Quilla>I know why it matters. That is why being treated as careless hurts.</v>

57
00:05:43.224 --> 00:05:45.324
<v Chitter>I do not know what else to believe.</v>

58
00:05:45.674 --> 00:05:48.605
<v Quilla>You could believe I am still your friend while we look.</v>

59
00:05:48.955 --> 00:05:58.595
<v Old Timber>The word gone sat between them. Chitter heard careless. Quilla heard liar. Neither word had actually been spoken.</v>

60
00:05:58.945 --> 00:06:08.965
<v Zippy>Okay. Timeline. Not blame-line. Timeline. We place only things somebody actually saw or heard.</v>

61
00:06:09.315 --> 00:06:12.017
<v Shelly>And we leave room for what nobody saw.</v>

62
00:06:12.367 --> 00:06:17.228
<v Garingo>I saw the return. Therefore I saw the complete truth.</v>

63
00:06:17.578 --> 00:06:19.378
<v Shelly>You saw one moment.</v>

64
00:06:19.728 --> 00:06:31.688
<v Zippy>Leaf one: Chitter lends pouch. Leaf two: Quilla carries pouch. Leaf three: Chitter finds no branch.</v>

65
00:06:32.038 --> 00:06:35.518
<v Chitter>Leaf four: Quilla says she returned it.</v>

66
00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:38.809
<v Quilla>Leaf four: Quilla returned it.</v>

67
00:06:39.159 --> 00:06:46.132
<v Zippy>Same leaf. Different sentence. We need the ten seconds between return and empty.</v>

68
00:06:46.482 --> 00:06:50.202
<v Bongo>I can search while you build sentences. I got this.</v>

69
00:06:50.552 --> 00:06:53.472
<v Bongo>Search one: under the flat stone.</v>

70
00:06:53.822 --> 00:07:00.902
<v Old Timber>He lifted it carefully. Beneath it was one annoyed beetle and no pouch.</v>

71
00:07:01.252 --> 00:07:05.278
<v Bongo>Sorry. Search two: behind the root.</v>

72
00:07:05.628 --> 00:07:09.818
<v Old Timber>Behind the root he found his own lunch, which seemed to have been searching for him.</v>

73
00:07:10.168 --> 00:07:16.288
<v Bongo>Good news for lunch. Search three: the grass marks where the branch was.</v>

74
00:07:16.638 --> 00:07:22.038
<v Old Timber>The marks ended after four steps. Whatever happened next had left the ground.</v>

75
00:07:22.388 --> 00:07:27.945
<v Garingo>A flying pouch. At last, the case respects my range.</v>

76
00:07:28.295 --> 00:07:30.032
<v Shelly>Or a carried branch.</v>

77
00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:34.662
<v Bongo>A carried branch. That sounds strangely familiar.</v>

78
00:07:35.012 --> 00:07:42.172
<v Old Timber>Bongo's smile faded. Chitter was staring at the bare stone, and Quilla had stopped meeting his eyes.</v>

79
00:07:42.522 --> 00:07:43.728
<v Chitter>I need a minute.</v>

80
00:07:44.078 --> 00:07:45.304
<v Quilla>So do I.</v>

81
00:07:46.013 --> 00:07:51.973
<v Old Timber>They sat on opposite sides of the flat stone while the oak-shadow crept closer through the grass.</v>

82
00:07:52.323 --> 00:07:59.471
<v Zippy>I can make a leaf called FEELINGS, but I suspect that would be a poor use of a very good leaf.</v>

83
00:07:59.821 --> 00:08:01.701
<v Shelly>Sit with us instead.</v>

84
00:08:02.051 --> 00:08:10.411
<v Old Timber>Zippy folded the unused leaf and sat. Garingo removed his badge. Bongo left his lunch where it was.</v>

85
00:08:10.761 --> 00:08:18.881
<v Chitter>It is not only the pouch. I let you carry something I keep close. When it was gone, it felt like my trust went too.</v>

86
00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:26.242
<v Quilla>When you asked the same question faster each time, it felt as if my answer counted less because it came from me.</v>

87
00:08:26.592 --> 00:08:35.672
<v Chitter>I was angry. I kept it quiet, but it was writing a bad story about you. I tried to get sure fast enough to stop being afraid.</v>

88
00:08:36.022 --> 00:08:46.202
<v Quilla>I was angry too. I left before I said something sharp. The pause was wise at first, but staying gone let my bad story grow.</v>

89
00:08:46.552 --> 00:08:54.432
<v Old Timber>A burr slipped from Quilla's fur and clicked against the stone. Bongo folded his paws over his lunch and waited.</v>

90
00:08:54.782 --> 00:09:01.604
<v Old Timber>I sat beside the stone and asked one question. What can you repair before the pouch is found?</v>

91
00:09:01.954 --> 00:09:06.570
<v Chitter>The part where I turned an empty place into proof that Quilla did not care.</v>

92
00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:11.228
<v Quilla>The part where I walked away instead of telling Chitter that his questions hurt me.</v>

93
00:09:11.578 --> 00:09:12.378
<v Old Timber>Mm.</v>

94
00:09:12.728 --> 00:09:19.801
<v Chitter>Quilla, I am sorry I treated my fear like proof. I should have asked what you saw and listened to the whole answer.</v>

95
00:09:20.151 --> 00:09:25.307
<v Chitter>I can ask God to help me slow down before fear turns a guess into proof.</v>

96
00:09:25.657 --> 00:09:33.730
<v Quilla>I am sorry I left you alone with the empty place. I should have said I was hurt instead of walking away and making you guess.</v>

97
00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:39.222
<v Quilla>I can ask God to help me come back after a pause and use kind words.</v>

98
00:09:39.572 --> 00:09:41.532
<v Chitter>I still want the pouch back.</v>

99
00:09:41.882 --> 00:09:46.438
<v Quilla>Of course. Repair does not require pretending it never mattered.</v>

100
00:09:46.788 --> 00:09:51.468
<v Chitter>Will you search with me? Even before we know which memory missed a piece?</v>

101
00:09:51.818 --> 00:09:54.948
<v Quilla>Yes. Side by side is a good place to look from.</v>

102
00:09:55.298 --> 00:09:59.716
<v Garingo>I also owe a repair. I announced more than I observed.</v>

103
00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:05.345
<v Garingo>I saw Quilla put the pouch on the branch. I did not see the pouch remain there.</v>

104
00:10:05.695 --> 00:10:09.146
<v Shelly>That is a smaller sentence and a better witness.</v>

105
00:10:09.496 --> 00:10:12.121
<v Garingo>My badge feels lighter already.</v>

106
00:10:12.471 --> 00:10:22.386
<v Zippy>Then we replay both accounts. Same ten seconds. No conclusions. Only sounds, movements, and exact words.</v>

107
00:10:22.736 --> 00:10:29.604
<v Chitter>My account first. I came from the seed shelf. I heard Gah-Ring-Goh say, RETURN OBSERVED.</v>

108
00:10:29.954 --> 00:10:37.141
<v Garingo>RETURN OBSERVED! Pouch secure! Branch present! Witness magnificent!</v>

109
00:10:37.491 --> 00:10:45.211
<v Chitter>I saw Quilla walking away. Then I looked at the stone. No branch. No pouch. That is all I saw.</v>

110
00:10:45.561 --> 00:10:52.507
<v Quilla>My account. I placed the strap over the branch fork. Three burrs caught the cloth, so I pulled them loose.</v>

111
00:10:52.857 --> 00:11:00.666
<v Quilla>Gah-Ring-Goh announced. I checked the knot. Then I walked away. I did not look behind the branch.</v>

112
00:11:01.016 --> 00:11:06.885
<v Zippy>Both accounts fit. The missing piece happened behind Quilla and before Chitter looked.</v>

113
00:11:07.591 --> 00:11:15.070
<v Garingo>Behind Quilla. After my announcement. There was a sound I rejected for lacking drama.</v>

114
00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.500
<v Shelly>What sound?</v>

115
00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:24.949
<v Garingo>Scritch. Thump. Scritch-scritch. Then Bongo said, left side, cooperate.</v>

116
00:11:25.299 --> 00:11:28.209
<v Bongo>That was me and the ambitious branch.</v>

117
00:11:28.559 --> 00:11:35.479
<v Bongo>I thought the smaller branch had been left behind, so I added it to the shade frame. I moved the return place.</v>

118
00:11:35.829 --> 00:11:45.426
<v Zippy>Then here are the whole ten seconds. Quilla loops the pouch over the fork. Three burrs catch. She pulls them loose.</v>

119
00:11:45.776 --> 00:11:53.367
<v Garingo>I announce the return and watch Quilla walk away. I hear branch sounds, but I do not turn around.</v>

120
00:11:53.717 --> 00:11:58.157
<v Shelly>Behind both of them, Bongo drags the large branch past the small one.</v>

121
00:11:58.507 --> 00:12:07.665
<v Bongo>The small fork catches the pouch strap. I lift both branches without seeing underneath, then carry the whole return place away.</v>

122
00:12:08.015 --> 00:12:14.855
<v Chitter>Then I arrive after the branch is gone. Every account was true, but none of us had the whole ten seconds.</v>

123
00:12:15.205 --> 00:12:20.030
<v Quilla>And the missing piece did not give us leave to hurt each other while we waited for it.</v>

124
00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.740
<v Chitter>You carried the whole here away.</v>

125
00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.537
<v Quilla>That would explain why here looked elsewhere.</v>

126
00:12:25.887 --> 00:12:33.662
<v Bongo>I am sorry. I listened when Chitter said not that branch, then carried exactly that branch.</v>

127
00:12:34.012 --> 00:12:37.417
<v Chitter>It was an accident. Help us check it carefully.</v>

128
00:12:37.767 --> 00:12:42.847
<v Bongo>Search three, continued. First, I lift the shade branch.</v>

129
00:12:43.197 --> 00:12:50.470
<v Old Timber>He lifted it. One acorn dropped onto his head. It had been waiting all afternoon for this moment.</v>

130
00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.980
<v Bongo>Second, I shake only the leaves.</v>

131
00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:59.968
<v Old Timber>One leaf landed on Shelly. Shelly studied it, then continued being Shelly beneath it.</v>

132
00:13:00.318 --> 00:13:03.478
<v Shelly>The leaf may stay. It has traveled enough.</v>

133
00:13:03.828 --> 00:13:06.828
<v Bongo>Third, I turn the branch slowly.</v>

134
00:13:07.178 --> 00:13:13.988
<v Old Timber>Under the fork, held against a patch of burrs, was a small brown pouch with one worried-looking knot.</v>

135
00:13:14.338 --> 00:13:15.388
<v Chitter>My pouch.</v>

136
00:13:15.738 --> 00:13:17.051
<v Quilla>Your pouch.</v>

137
00:13:17.401 --> 00:13:19.881
<v Chitter>And the repair happened before it came back.</v>

138
00:13:20.231 --> 00:13:23.921
<v Quilla>Good. I would not want a pouch doing all our friendship work.</v>

139
00:13:24.271 --> 00:13:32.146
<v Garingo>Then I revise the official record. Two honest accounts. One missing branch. Zero villains.</v>

140
00:13:32.496 --> 00:13:37.341
<v Zippy>And one timeline with a label called THINGS WE DID NOT KNOW YET.</v>

141
00:13:37.691 --> 00:13:38.834
<v Shelly>Keep that leaf.</v>

142
00:13:39.184 --> 00:13:42.024
<v Bongo>Can the ambitious branch keep its job?</v>

143
00:13:42.374 --> 00:13:45.294
<v Chitter>Yes. Far away from pouch-return duties.</v>

144
00:13:45.644 --> 00:13:46.966
<v Garingo>And my badge?</v>

145
00:13:47.316 --> 00:13:49.996
<v Shelly>It may return to being a leaf.</v>

146
00:13:50.346 --> 00:13:51.964
<v Garingo>A grand rest.</v>

147
00:13:52.674 --> 00:13:58.634
<v Old Timber>That evening, beside the pond, I asked what had nearly done more harm than the missing pouch.</v>

148
00:13:58.984 --> 00:14:02.520
<v Chitter>The angry story I kept adding to while I stayed quiet.</v>

149
00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:07.701
<v Quilla>And my silence, once it stopped being a pause and became a wall.</v>

150
00:14:08.051 --> 00:14:11.091
<v Garingo>Also certainty wearing a leaf badge.</v>

151
00:14:11.441 --> 00:14:21.703
<v Old Timber>Mm. A man named Paul once wrote to friends in Ephesus. His letter is in the Bible, in Ephesians, chapter four, verse twenty-six.</v>

152
00:14:22.053 --> 00:14:29.773
<v Old Timber>In the King James Version, it says, Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:</v>

153
00:14:30.123 --> 00:14:37.763
<v Quilla>The line does not pretend anger is not there. It asks us not to let anger become the thing that chooses harm.</v>

154
00:14:38.113 --> 00:14:46.642
<v Chitter>Wrath is an old word for anger we hold onto until it grows hard and wants to do harm. Mine grew each time I added a guess.</v>

155
00:14:46.992 --> 00:14:56.544
<v Old Timber>That is it. God did not ask them to erase the feeling or excuse the mistake. He helped them keep hurt from deciding what happened next.</v>

156
00:14:56.894 --> 00:15:00.694
<v Shelly>And it left room for the missing piece to arrive without needing a villain.</v>

157
00:15:01.396 --> 00:15:09.356
<v Old Timber>Professor Hoot, our owl, set one claw beside the burrs and looked across the flat stone as though it were a lecture hall.</v>

158
00:15:09.706 --> 00:15:16.992
<v Professor Hoot>A burr can carry many tiny hooks. Those hooks catch on loops in fur or cloth and help the seed travel.</v>

159
00:15:17.342 --> 00:15:20.582
<v Bongo>That pouch traveled far too well.</v>

160
00:15:20.932 --> 00:15:27.720
<v Professor Hoot>A human inventor named George de Mestral looked closely at burrs after they stuck to fur and clothing.</v>

161
00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:38.162
<v Professor Hoot>He copied the hook-and-loop idea to make a fastener that can open and close again. Learning that way from nature is called biomimicry.</v>

162
00:15:38.512 --> 00:15:39.831
<v Bongo>What does that mean?</v>

163
00:15:40.181 --> 00:15:47.338
<v Professor Hoot>It means noticing how a living thing solves a problem, then using that lesson to design something helpful.</v>

164
00:15:47.688 --> 00:15:50.664
<v Garingo>My leaf badge was inspired by leaves.</v>

165
00:15:51.014 --> 00:15:57.777
<v Professor Hoot>That is wearing a leaf. You must learn how a living thing works, not only wear it. Class refined.</v>

166
00:15:58.479 --> 00:16:11.479
<v Old Timber>The reeds shook once. Splish, Splash, and Splosh, the three frog brothers, slid to the pond edge in a row that lasted half a second. Mudpuppy Minutes had begun.</v>

167
00:16:11.829 --> 00:16:15.229
<v Splosh>Today on Mudpuppy Minutes: why does your stomach growl?</v>

168
00:16:15.579 --> 00:16:18.579
<v Splish>A tiny bear inside you is moving the lunch furniture.</v>

169
00:16:18.929 --> 00:16:23.479
<v Splash>Incorrect! Your breakfast is knocking because it forgot the password.</v>

170
00:16:23.829 --> 00:16:32.335
<v Splosh>Or muscles in your digestive system move food, liquid, and gas along. Those movements can make growling sounds.</v>

171
00:16:32.685 --> 00:16:35.747
<v Splish>Oh no. That answer has a school word in it.</v>

172
00:16:36.097 --> 00:16:39.289
<v Splash>Put the school word in a hat and ask the bear.</v>

173
00:16:39.639 --> 00:16:43.839
<v Splosh>The hat says the bear is called Sir Rumbles.</v>

174
00:16:44.189 --> 00:16:46.826
<v Splish>So an empty stomach is rehearsing for lunch.</v>

175
00:16:47.176 --> 00:16:49.696
<v Splash>Mine rehearses during quiet time.</v>

176
00:16:50.046 --> 00:16:55.366
<v Splosh>That is excellent timing for a stomach and poor timing for everyone else.</v>

177
00:16:55.716 --> 00:16:59.419
<v Splosh>The bear says the password is sandwich.</v>

178
00:16:59.769 --> 00:17:04.369
<v Splish>Too easy. The bear must knock three times and wiggle its ears.</v>

179
00:17:04.719 --> 00:17:08.260
<v Splash>What if the bear has very serious ears?</v>

180
00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:14.890
<v Splosh>Mudpuppies, mudpuppies, we have solved it. Stomachs growl when the lunch door forgets the ear wiggle.</v>

181
00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.699
<v Splish>And a bear rearranges the chairs.</v>

182
00:17:18.049 --> 00:17:20.569
<v Splash>Quietly. It lives there.</v>

183
00:17:20.919 --> 00:17:22.431
<v Splish>Does the bear pay rent?</v>

184
00:17:22.781 --> 00:17:32.341
<v Old Timber>Your digestive system uses muscles to move food, liquid, and gas. Those movements can make a growling sound, especially when your stomach is empty.</v>

185
00:17:32.691 --> 00:17:38.411
<v Old Timber>No tiny bear, lunch furniture, secret knock, or ear wiggle is required.</v>

186
00:17:39.117 --> 00:17:47.867
<v Old Timber>When anger grows, you may need a pause. Ask a trusted grown-up for help, then return to safe repair when you can speak without harm.</v>

187
00:17:48.217 --> 00:17:51.898
<v Chitter>And label one leaf THINGS WE DO NOT KNOW YET.</v>

188
00:17:52.248 --> 00:17:58.848
<v Old Timber>The pond is quiet again. I am Old Timber, and I will meet you beside the next question.</v>

189
00:17:59.198 --> 00:18:02.428
<v Ranger Ray>See you next time, somewhere in Shiloh Creek.</v>
